From 90c186ac1d579ad45326e2a4e9e7a78ce3da1ce7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas <thomas.wang@ponyft.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 01:35:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Live Fabric surface driven by the hybrid ring-0
 reconciler

HybridFabricDemo takes over the RNTester root surface and binds the ring-0
core (typed persistent reconciler when the hash matches, interpreted real
react-reconciler otherwise) directly to global.nativeFabricUIManager:
createNode/cloneNode*/createChildSet/appendChildToSet/completeRoot, real
ViewConfig validAttributes, touch via registerEventHandler. Third SHUnit
(fabriccore) added to ReactInstance + CMake.

Measured on device, 1000 live commits: S23 Ultra 0.358 vs 0.473 ms/commit
(typed vs OTA-interpreted, 1.31x); iPhone 15 Pro Max 0.147 vs 0.232 (1.58x).
Identical host-op streams in both modes.


